# My everyday loaf based on morph

starter:
  ap_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter = 20g
  bread_flour
  cold_water
  hydration = 100%

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  barley
  spelt
  buckwheat

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

wet:
  cold_water
  flourless_starter = 10%
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 2g
  leaven = 40%
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  hydration = 70%
  # 200g/L of flour
  # total_flour = 660g # 13 inch
  total_flour = 500g # 9 inch

/*
July 27, 2026

Changes
- Only 9g of starter remaining!
- Mix a larger than needed leaven and use the rest for starter

Zoji pan weighs 773g. KA pan weighs 725g.

Starter is 8 days old.

Mixed the leaven about 16:20 left on the counter. Initial T is 76.4.

Leaven pH = 4.5 at 7:25 dt is 60.7F. Is it the reduced innoculation
or lowered temp that made the difference?

The flourless starter pH is 3.3 less than 24 hours after making it.

I started about 7:20

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 7:53. Stopped after 3 minutes.
DT after mixing is 72F. RT is 78F. 

30 minute rest in fridge.

Kneaded 8 minutes in KA.

Into the cambro and the fridge at 8:44. S&F every 30 minutes.

Out of the fridge at 9:50, dT is 59F. Left on counter to relax.

Into the pan at 10:20. DT is 68F. Left on the counter at 78F.

Baked at 11:47 for 45 minutes at 350F lid off.

I added 150ml of water to the pan before preheating the oven.

5.25 inches tall. Beautiful crust. The alternating diagonal slashes
look good. 

Super soft and delicious. Less sour than the last one.

*/

